    declaration: struct-decl #46 2565:50:1-3528:68:1 name="@2::Connection" doc="An HTTP/1.1 connection that the program drives itself, as `Net::HTTP.start` gives: one request at a time, and the\nbody read piece by piece. Open it with `start`, send with `send_request`, read with `read_body` and end it with\n`finish`. The fields are the connection's own: do not read them. It belongs to the task that opened it, as a socket\ndoes, and one call at a time uses it."
      field: field-decl #31 2628:52:3-2647:53:1 name="socket" doc="The socket, a plain one or a TLS one."
        type: type-ref #30 2636:52:11-2646:52:21 name="TCP.Socket"
      field: field-decl #33 2726:54:3-2741:55:1 name="scheme" doc="`http` or `https`, the host and the port, which the request head names."
        type: type-ref #32 2734:54:11-2740:54:17 name="String"
      field: field-decl #35 2743:55:3-2756:56:1 name="host"
        type: type-ref #34 2749:55:9-2755:55:15 name="String"
      field: field-decl #37 2758:56:3-2768:57:1 name="port"
        type: type-ref #36 2764:56:9-2767:56:12 name="Int"
      field: field-decl #39 3063:60:3-3095:61:1 name="options" doc="The options it was opened with: `timeout_ms` is the time of each `send_request` (the write and the head),\n`read_timeout_ms` the time of each `read_body`, and `max_body_bytes` the largest request body. A `proxy` has no\nuser info here, so printing a connection shows no password."
        type: type-ref #38 3072:60:12-3094:60:34 name="HttpWire.ClientOptions"
      field: field-decl #42 3291:63:3-3314:64:1 name="login" doc="The `Proxy-Authorization` value of the proxy's user info (\"\" with none), alone in a channel that holds one value:\na channel prints as `<Channel>`, where a field would print the login."
